Z||000000||ThatRickGuy||02-09-2001||02:42 PM||||One project at a time, ah? well the front end is done  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> next up is the exhaust, starting at the manifolds, so 2 questions.<P>There was someone posting a few months ago who mentioned selling bored out manifolds, just wondering about a POC for that. Thanks.<P>And, is it advisable to take out the rear 2 carrige bolts (on an 88) and lift the car some to get more access to the inboard manifold? <P>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||02-09-2001||10:33 PM||||Congratulations on the finishing the front end.  Been there done that.  I am just completing the manifold welding, porting and reinstalling on one of our 88s. It not too bad. Yes, you can remove the rear bolt with a jack holding things up and slowly lower it to gain room. Here a link for someone who will port your manifold on and exchange basis.  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/006593.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/006593.html</A>   Good luck and happy Fieroing.||||reg||1
